cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software itself and the accompanying paper."
title: "TAMIA: Edge Computing System for Real-Time Weather Radar Reflectivity"
abstract: >-
  TAMIA (Tropical Andean Meteorological Imaging Architecture) is a three-layer
  edge-cloud system for real-time processing and visualization of the horizontal
  reflectivity field (DBZH) of weather radars. Edge nodes co-located with each
  radar run the full DBZH pipeline locally — multi-elevation compositing,
  adaptive ground-clutter correction and polar-to-Cartesian projection with
  explicit WGS84 bounds — and upload only the resulting georeferenced PNG to a
  central FastAPI + PostgreSQL service, which pushes it to a React + Leaflet web
  viewer over WebSocket. Deployed on the LOXX and GUAXX X-band radars of the
  RadarNet-Sur network in southern Ecuador. "Tamia" means "rain" in Kichwa.
